Here is how to get rogue running on VMS:1) unpack these sources -- if you have them in vms_share format,   concatenate the different files in correct order into somefile.com,   then type @somefile; if you have them in cshar format, you will   either have to extract them on a UNIX system and then send them   to your VMS system somehow, or manually unpack the files with   your favorite editor.  (Ugh!)2) once you have all the files in one source directory, type	@make   to compile and link everything together.  Alternatively you   could use the VMS make program available from either of the   following anonymous FTP sites:	SITE:	pomona.claremont.edu	IP-#:	134.173.4.160	DIR:	[.utilities.make]	FILES:	*.*	SITE:	vmsd.oac.uci.edu	IP-#:	128.200.15.2	DIR:	/	FILES:	make_src.*   [Makefile.vms was generated by this make program]   Install it at your site and type	rename Makefile.vms  Makefile	make   Either way, you may now play rogue by typing	rogue   but if you want to do it every session, you should put the   following into your LOGIN.COM:	$ rogue :== $DISK:[DIRECTORY]rogue.exe   for example I might have	$ rogue :== $DISK$USER26:[MZRALY.ROGUE]   If you have any questions, try typing	help :=--Mike Zraly				``Times are bad.  Children no longermzraly@ldbvax.dnet.lotus.com		  obey their parents, and everyone isor c/o seaotter@athena.mit.edu		  writing a book.'' -- Cicero